message: "If you reference or use this software in your research or educational work, please cite it as below."
title: "LOB.0: Reinforcement Learning-Driven Adaptive Market Making Engine"
authors:
  - family-names: "Saurav"
    given-names: "Student Researcher"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-07
url: "https://github.com/sumansuman1212/LOB.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sumansuman1212/LOB.0"
keywords:
  - "market microstructure"
  - "limit order book"
  - "reinforcement learning"
  - "proximal policy optimization"
  - "algorithmic trading"
  - "high-frequency trading"
  - "quantitative finance"
  - "systems programming"
  - "C++17"
abstract: >-
  LOB.0 is an educational and research-oriented quantitative trading system combining
  an ultra-low-latency C++17 limit order book execution engine with a Python (PyTorch)
  reinforcement learning harness. The engine evaluates order-flow imbalance (OFI),
  Welford rolling realized volatility, and inventory risk to generate adaptive bid/ask
  quotes with hard risk guardrails.
